            <ArticleTitle>Idiosyncratic reaction to intracoronary injection of non-ionic contrast media.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>396-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Four patients who developed coronary artery spasm in response to their first intracoronary injection of a non-ionic contrast agent, either iopamidol or iohexol, are described. It is suggested that this idiosyncratic reaction may be related to the non-ionic character of these contrast media.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
